 "about": "Pyrenean oak above all, from the valleys to the treeline; sweet chestnut groves in El Bierzo, Sanabria, Trás-os-Montes and the Sistema Central, pedunculate oak in the damp western valleys, holm oak and a little cork oak on warm slopes and in the gorges, Portuguese oak on the limestone rim of Burgos, beech in the Demanda, downy birch in the high valleys, ash, alder and poplar along the meadows and rivers, eucalyptus on the low Portuguese and Galician fringe; maritime and Scots pine plantations, and native Scots pine in the Demanda and Gredos; common, white Spanish and purging broom, tree heath, gum rockrose and gorse on the hills, prickly juniper in the gorges and dwarf juniper above the treeline; heather, bracken, bilberry, mat-grass and white asphodel on the ground; brown cattle, large sheep flocks, goats, horses on the heath and Iberian ibex on the Gredos rocks. Hawthorn stands in for the cherry, apple and pear orchards.",
